ave to pass a  constitutional test that balances  privacy rights with Public Health to put  bracelets on people under any  circumstances would require that a law  be passed and  I do not believe that the emergency  management powers allow either federal  or provincial legislatures to do that  right now  Hong Kong supposedly had 20,000  bracelets ready at airport arrivals but  not everyone received one I think one  big problem is that they really didn't  have a chance to test run the whole  system before it goes out Tracy is  working out the kinks so to speak but  feels this is the way to get out of  lockdown faster once the tracking is  over you cut the bracelet off and it's  done this is not a a sort of behind your  back Big Brother sort of thing still the  concern over Big Brother may explain why  Canada is relying on the conscience of  Canadians to prevent communities spread  of this silent killer  doctors in Japan are warning that the  country's medical system could collapse  amid a wave of nuke ovid 19 cases Japan  initially appeared to have the virus  under control but now there are more  than 10,000 confirmed cases of Cova 19  in the country  health officials say emergency rooms  have been unable to treat some patients  with serious health conditions because  of the extra burden caused by the virus  pandemic pets how our time staying home  is helping more animals find homes  that's next  we've all been spending a lot more time  at home this past month seeing our  friends on screens instead of in person  animal shelters are seeing a huge  increase in the number of people looking  to adopt or foster a pet to deal with  the loneliness from Cova 19 it was  Reggie Cecchini the need to find these  animals a forever home has run up  against a world stuck at home as the  copic 19 pandemic leaves shelters  struggle to keep their doors open the  staff person goes down with kovat then  what does that mean for the team that  they've got in place to deal with the  frontli